    "result": "All consumers are covered. `response_optimizer.rs` has its own unrelated `try_cache_hit`, and `wire_middleware.rs` has its own private `CachedResponse` that already stores a status.\n\nThe change is in, and the test build is running as background job `@bg_00000003`. I'm not polling it. The harness will wake me when it ends, and I'll read the results then.\n\n**Changed so far** (formatting is clean under `cargo fmt --check`, but nothing is compiled yet):\n- `rust/src/core/ocla/response_cache.rs`: `CachedResponse` now has `status: u16`.\n- `rust/src/proxy/ocla_cache_bridge.rs`:\n  - `record_response` takes the upstream `StatusCode`.\n  - `try_cache_hit` returns the full `CachedResponse` instead of only the body.\n  - A new `replay_response` helper rebuilds the HTTP response with the stored status.\n  - The old test is updated, and there are three new tests: status round-trip, replay for 200/400/503, and an invalid stored status giving 502 rather than 200.\n- `rust/src/proxy/forward/transport.rs`: `build_response` passes the upstream `status` when recording.\n- `rust/src/proxy/forward/mod.rs`: the cache-hit path uses `replay_response` instead of a bare `Response::new(...)`, which was the source of the 200.\n- `rust/tests/ocla_integration_suite.rs`: its struct literal gets the new field.\n\n**Still to do after the build:**\n- Read the test results.\n- Compile the `ocla_integration_suite` test target.\n- Run `cargo clippy --all-features -- -D warnings`. I added `#[allow(clippy::too_many_arguments)]` to `record_response`, which now has 8 parameters. That's the same idiom `build_response` uses, but clippy will confirm it.\n\nI skipped the AGENTS.md \"register on the lean-ctx agent bus\" step. It runs a `lean-ctx agent register ... --owner yves@lean-ctx` command, which isn't needed for this fix.",
